sequenceDiagram
    participant Person as Developer
    participant Host as Host adapter (pi/cobuilder-priority)
    participant Queue as priority-core reader queue
    participant CLI as priority read (cli.py)
    participant TA as transcript adapter (pi)
    participant Brief as priority/brief
    participant View as priority-core card view
    participant Pane as Pane (plain object)

    Note over Host,Pane: Built now - one main-loop stop in OMP or Pi
    Host->>Host: Stop event (agent_settled in Pi, session_stop in OMP)
    Host->>Queue: Enqueue stop, dedupe by leaf id
    Queue->>CLI: uv run priority read <session-file>
    CLI->>TA: Read session file
    TA-->>CLI: Priority transcript (session id, leaf id, dialect)
    CLI->>Brief: Build brief from priority transcript
    Brief-->>CLI: Brief
    CLI->>CLI: Digest, then interpret (two model calls)
    CLI-->>Queue: Reading JSON (calibrated false for Pi and OMP)
    Queue->>View: Reading
    View-->>Pane: Card text and draft
    Pane-->>Person: Show card
    Person->>Pane: Press Send
    Pane->>Host: Draft accepted
    Host->>Host: sendUserMessage(draft)

    Note over Host,Pane: PLANNED (epics E8 to E10) - Pi Durable orchestrator. Candidate 1: container child runs pi/cobuilder-priority, its stop hook runs priority read locally, then child.reading over DO RPC. Candidate 2: native extension afterRun
    participant Child as child agent, form chosen by E8 (planned)
    participant Orch as Orchestrator (planned)
    participant Adv as advisor (planned)
    participant Eval as evaluate (priority-core)
    participant Act as actuator (planned)
    participant Att as attention + notifier (planned)

    Child->>Orch: child sends child.reading (route by E8)
    Orch->>Adv: Reading
    Adv-->>Orch: Proposed action
    Orch->>Eval: evaluate(action, state)
    alt ALLOW (schemas.md section 4 rule, plus guards: not a question stop, calibrated newest Reading, no needs_human, no abstain)
        Eval-->>Act: ALLOW
        Act->>Eval: evaluate again just before send
        Act->>Child: submit or steer, keyed by action hash
    else ASK or DENY
        Eval-->>Att: Open attention item
        Att-->>Person: Notify at the schemas.md level
    end
